445	 * DECODES the slug/family before lookup (2026-09-24 fix — see
446	 * docs/DOCUMENTATION.md's dated entry): a page.tsx dynamic route segment
447	 * that also exports `generateStaticParams` gets its `params` value as the
448	 * STILL-PERCENT-ENCODED path segment in this Next.js version (confirmed
449	 * live: requesting `/mods/minecraft/abyss+` — or the equivalently-encoded
450	 * `/mods/minecraft/abyss%2B` — makes `params.slug` arrive as the literal
451	 * string `"abyss%2B"`, not `"abyss+"`; a plain Route Handler on the exact
452	 * same path shape decodes correctly, so this is specific to the
453	 * generateStaticParams + page.tsx combination). Real catalogue slugs
454	 * legitimately contain `+`, `,`, `` ` ``, `"` (Modrinth project slugs are
455	 * not sanitized at import) — 377 of them 404'd because of this. Tries the
456	 * decoded value first (the common, now-fixed case), then falls back to the
457	 * raw value passed in (covers the rare slug that is itself the literal
458	 * string containing a `%`, and keeps this function correct for callers that
459	 * already pass a clean, non-encoded value — decoding twice is a no-op for
460	 * any string with no percent-escapes in it).
